      "writtenOn": "2021-01-13T01:38:39Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I thought the system would be using a SignalStrengthUpdateRequest() object going forward too (to encapsulate the SignalThresholdInfo objects)? In which case, still can\u0027t just be checked here. The instance/use-case specific checking has to be done in the binder call in PhoneInterfaceManager(). That\u0027s where we will have to validate system vs end-user anyway since that\u0027s the security boundary.\n\nSomehow I think it\u0027ll be cleaner in the end if you have something like:\nvalidateForUser() and validateForSystem() based on the Binder.getCallingUid().\n\nThink about it. I know there are more patches coming, so perhaps it\u0027ll be easier for me to see what you\u0027re thinking once I see the PhoneInterfaceManager and ServiceStateTracker code.",
